      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-148768",
      ":question/problem": "Let $f(x)$ be negative and strictly decreasing for $x \u2208 [2, 4]$, and differentiable for $x \u2208 (2, 4)$. Suppose we approximate the area under the curve $y = g(x) = (1 - x) \\cdot f(x)$ over the interval $[2, 4]$ using a right Riemann sum. Given that $g(x) > 0$, which of the following statements must be true?\n\n1. $f^{\u2032}(x) > 0$\n2. $g^{\u2032}(x) > 0$\n3. The Riemann sum underestimates the true area."
